  "problem": "Let $V={R}_{2}[t],$ the vector space of real polynomials of degree at most $2,$ and let the inner product on $V$ be defined as\n\n$$\n⟨p(t),q(t)⟩=p(-1)q(-1)+p(0)q(0)+p(1)q(1).\n$$\n\nNow consider the following elements of $V:$\n\n$$\n{p}_{1}(t)={t}^{2}-t,\\,{p}_{2}(t)={t}^{2}+t,\\,q(t)=4{t}^{2}-t-1\n$$\n\nFind the orthogonal projection of $q(t)$ onto $S=\\text{Span}\\{{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t)\\}$ given that ${p}_{1}(t)⊥{p}_{2}(t)$ with respect to the inner product, and that the orthogonal projection of $q(t)$ onto $\\text{Span}\\{{p}_{1}(t)\\}$ equals $2{t}^{2}-2t.$",
